## About the standard

SSF 200 concerns the physical security of buildings and premises. Protection classes 1–3 describe the required level of protection for elements such as walls, doors, windows, locks, and other parts of the building envelope.

The standard does not cover the design of intruder alarms or surveillance systems. Those systems are assessed against other requirements, such as SSF 130 for intruder and hold-up alarms.

Official source: [SSF 200 utgåva 6](https://www.stoldskyddsforeningen.se/butik/foretag/ssf-normer/skal-inbrottsskydd/ssf-200-utg-6-regler-for-inbrottsskydd-byggnader-och-lokaler/).
